xf.tutorial.open_menu=Open Xenofactions Menu
xf.tutorial.page0=Welcome to the Xenofactions command GUI. Press K by default to open it. You can change this key in Minecraft Options, Controls, under the Xenofactions category.
xf.tutorial.page1=The menu groups commands into categories such as Faction, Members, Territory, Cities, War, Economy, TDM, Admin, and Help. Use the global search field to find commands by name, alias, description, or legacy usage.
xf.tutorial.page2=Command forms show argument fields and searchable list choices when the server can provide safe data such as players, factions, members, applicants, allies, enemies, warps, cities, and flags. Text fields remain available when a list is unavailable.
xf.tutorial.page3=Always inspect the command preview before using Run Command. Open in Chat puts the generated slash command in chat, and Copy Usage copies the exact legacy usage. Dangerous commands ask for one extra GUI confirmation.
xf.tutorial.page4=The server still validates every command, permission, faction rank, cooldown, and config rule. Legacy slash commands still work: /c help, /c create New_Faction, /c claim Capital, /c sethome, /c balance, /c war Enemy_Faction, /c peace Enemy_Faction, and /c help (Non-ADMIN) / /xc help (ADMIN/OP). Faction spaces may require underscores in legacy commands. Reopen this tutorial from the main menu.
